<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ryukyuans</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ryukyuan people, Okinawans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ryukyuans are the Indigenous people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryukyu-islands">Ryukyu Islands</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a>, today mostly part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/okinawa-prefecture">Okinawa Prefecture</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. They formed the Ryukyu Kingdom, which traded widely with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, Japan and South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>, and they speak Ryukyuan languages related to Japanese. Japan annexed their islands in 1879.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ryukyuans.jpg" alt="Ryukyuans" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Pierre Dalbéra from Paris, France · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Danses_d%E2%80%99Okinawa_(mus%C3%A9e_Guimet,_Paris)_(11152072573).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
